Creating Stories and Epics
🔐 Before You Create ANYTHING - ID Verification Checklist
STOP! Before creating a story, verify:

□ I'm using customfield_10972 for TEAM assignment
  └─ Valid IDs: 11559, 11560, or 11561 ONLY

□ I'm using customfield_10970 for COMPONENT assignment  
  └─ Valid IDs: 11554, 11555, 11556, 11557, or 11558 ONLY

□ I have NOT mixed up these two fields

□ Both fields are present in additionalAttributes
If you can't check ALL boxes above, DO NOT proceed with creation!

Basic Story Creation
Stories in the CCE project require: 1. A Super-Team assignment (customfield_10972) - MUST be 11559, 11560, or 11561 2. A Component assignment (customfield_10970) - MUST be 11554-11558 3. An Epic link (parentIssueId) if linking to an epic

Example: Creating a Single Story
cat > /tmp/story.json << 'EOF'
{
  "projectKey": "CCE",
  "type": "Story",
  "summary": "API: Implement user authentication",
  "description": {
    "content": [
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Implement JWT-based authentication for the API endpoints.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc",
    "version": 1
  },
  "parentIssueId": "CCE-55",
  "additionalAttributes": {
    "customfield_10972": {
      "id": "11560"
    },
    "customfield_10970": {
      "id": "11554"
    }
  }
}
EOF

acli jira workitem create --from-json /tmp/story.json
Explanation: - projectKey: The Jira project key (CCE) - type: Story, Task, Bug, or Epic - summary: The issue title - description: Must use ADF format (see below) - parentIssueId: Links to an epic (e.g., "CCE-55") - customfield_10972: TEAM field - use "11560" (Control-Freaks), "11559" (Stallions), or "11561" (Infra) - ⚠️ DO NOT use 11554-11558 here - those are component IDs! - customfield_10970: COMPONENT field - use "11554" (Control Interface), "11555" (Aave), "11556" (Cooper), "11557" (Canton/Cumberland), or "11558" (Infra) - ⚠️ DO NOT use 11559-11561 here - those are team IDs!

Atlassian Document Format (ADF)
ADF is Jira Cloud's rich text format. You must use ADF JSON for descriptions, not plain text or wiki markup.

Basic ADF Structure
{
  "version": 1,
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    // Array of content nodes (paragraphs, headings, lists, etc.)
  ]
}
Common ADF Elements
Paragraph
{
  "type": "paragraph",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is a paragraph."
    }
  ]
}
Heading (h2-h6)
{
  "type": "heading",
  "attrs": {"level": 2},
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Section Heading"
    }
  ]
}
Bold Text
{
  "type": "text",
  "text": "Bold text",
  "marks": [{"type": "strong"}]
}
Bullet List
{
  "type": "bulletList",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "listItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "First item"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "listItem",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Second item"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
Numbered List
