Common Pitfalls and Solutions
🚨 ❌ Problem #1: Using WRONG IDs in WRONG Fields (MOST COMMON ERROR!)
Symptoms: - Story creation fails silently - Fields appear empty in Jira - No clear error message

Root Cause: Using a Team ID (11559-11561) in the Component field, or a Component ID (11554-11558) in the Team field.

❌ WRONG - This LOOKS correct but will FAIL:

"additionalAttributes": {
  "customfield_10972": {"id": "11558"},  ← WRONG! 11558 is Infra COMPONENT, not a team
  "customfield_10970": {"id": "11561"}   ← WRONG! 11561 is Infra TEAM, not a component
}
✅ CORRECT - Match IDs to the right field:

"additionalAttributes": {
  "customfield_10972": {"id": "11561"},  ← CORRECT! Team field gets a TEAM ID
  "customfield_10970": {"id": "11558"}   ← CORRECT! Component field gets a COMPONENT ID
}
Memory Aid: - customfield_10972 (ends in 72) = TEAM assignment (who owns it) - customfield_10970 (ends in 70) = COMPONENT assignment (what it affects)

Quick Validation: - Team IDs: 11559, 11560, 11561 (only 3 options) - Component IDs: 11554, 11555, 11556, 11557, 11558 (5 options) - If you put a team ID (11559-61) in customfield_10970, it's WRONG! - If you put a component ID (11554-58) in customfield_10972, it's WRONG!

❌ Problem #2: "Component is required" error
Cause: Missing one or both required custom fields

Solution: Always include BOTH custom fields in additionalAttributes:

"additionalAttributes": {
  "customfield_10972": {"id": "11560"},  ← TEAM field (required)
  "customfield_10970": {"id": "11554"}   ← COMPONENT field (required)
}
❌ Problem #3: "INVALID_INPUT" when editing
Solution: When using --from-json for edits, include the issues array:

{
  "issues": ["CCE-55"],
  "description": { ... }
}
❌ Problem #4: Description shows raw ADF JSON
Solution: Don't pass ADF as a string to --description. Use JSON file with proper structure.

❌ Problem #5: "Cannot set field 'labels'" error
Solution: The CCE project doesn't support labels on creation. Remove labels from your JSON.

❌ Problem #6: Wiki markup not rendering
Solution: Jira Cloud uses ADF, not wiki markup. Convert to ADF JSON format.

